"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[95905],{495905:n=>{n.exports='# Performance Tuning — Hints and Indexes\n\nSource dialect query hints, index hints, and statistics operations that have no DBSQL equivalent, plus what to drop vs. translate.\n\n> This doc is dialect-agnostic for the "what to drop" rules. The MSSQL section covers what to substitute.\n\n## What to drop unconditionally\n\nThese hints/options have no equivalent in DBSQL and must be removed without substitution:\n\n| Source                                                | Remove                                     |\n| ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------ |\n| `WITH (NOLOCK)`                                       | DBSQL MVCC is always non-blocking; remove  |\n| `WITH (ROWLOCK)`, `WITH (PAGELOCK)`, `WITH (TABLOCK)` | No row/page/table locks in DBSQL           |\n| `OPTION (RECOMPILE)`                                  | Query plan management is automatic         |\n| `OPTION (MAXDOP n)`                                   | Parallelism managed automatically by Spark |\n| `SET STATISTICS IO ON`                                | No equivalent; use `EXPLAIN` instead       |\n| `SET STATISTICS TIME ON`                              | No equivalent; use query profiler          |\n| `UPDATE STATISTICS`, `sp_updatestats`                 | Delta handles statistics automatically     |\n| `DBCC FREEPROCCACHE`, `DBCC DROPCLEANBUFFERS`         | No equivalent; cache managed automatically |\n| `INDEX = n` (index hints)                             | No index hints; Delta uses data skipping   |\n| `FORCESCAN`, `FORCESEEK`                              | No equivalent                              |\n\n## What to translate\n\n| Source                            | DBSQL equivalent                                            |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Clustered index on sort key       | `CLUSTER BY (col)` (liquid clustering) or `ZORDER BY (col)` |\n| Covering index for lookup         | `OPTIMIZE ... ZORDER BY (lookup_col)`                       |\n| Partitioned table for range scans | `PARTITIONED BY (date_col)` in CREATE TABLE                 |\n| Columnstore index                 | Delta is columnar by default; no explicit equivalent needed |\n\n## MSSQL\n\n```sql\n-- T-SQL with hints → DBSQL equivalents\nSELECT * FROM orders WITH (NOLOCK)       -- → SELECT * FROM orders\nJOIN customers WITH (NOLOCK) ON ...      -- → JOIN customers ON ...\nOPTION (RECOMPILE, MAXDOP 4)            -- → (remove OPTION clause entirely)\n```\n\nZ-ORDER for frequently filtered columns:\n\n```sql\nOPTIMIZE orders ZORDER BY (customer_id, order_date);\n```\n\n## SYNAPSE\n\nSame as MSSQL. Synapse-specific distribution and statistics hints (`DISTRIBUTION = HASH(...)`, `WITH STATISTICS_NORECOMPUTE`) have no DBSQL equivalent — remove them.\n'}}]);
